{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/261190-demon-auras","id":261190,"title":"Demon Auras","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-20T04:34:47-07:00","id":261190,"title":"Demon Auras","content":"I read under the 'Aura Sight' demonic power that demons are perceived as having 'Wire cables coming off of them' for their auras (assuming of course you are able to get past their Cover). I'm just curious if there is any more detail on this, and if Stigmatics and Angels have been given similar treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3910-lord_salamander","name":"Lord_Salamander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T10:23:13-07:00","id":261353,"title":"","content":"Stigmatic definitely, a but remember, demons can Spoof any effect that would reveal themselves to be anything other than an ordinary human. Unless they fail that Spoof roll all an Aura Sight will get is 'Perfectly normal human, needs more vegetables in his diet, probably a Libra.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T11:50:00-07:00","id":261385,"title":"","content":"But now I must wonder does the demon not require to be aware of necessity to spoof? It would make sence in a way to be a reflex but then it would require a rational. I forget the concepts name but 'the act of observation changes the results'. You could tell them they feel the need to spoof and then they can choose to spoof or risk being seen.<br /> <br /> the reason I find it interesting this way is simple, &quot;the hairs on the back of your neck stand on end. Do you chose to spoof?&quot; Just how much suspense that could add to a scene!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T12:17:35-07:00","id":261399,"title":"","content":"Demon spoofing is a reflexive action and the demon does not need to be aware of the revealing effect or even specifically targeted which can be quite terrifying to know someone in the area can sense you if you make one bad roll and have no idea who","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3839-crytofloragardener","name":"CrytofloraGardener","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T14:05:51-07:00","id":261467,"title":"","content":"Thank you I was hoping I was remembering that wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T16:32:31-07:00","id":261584,"title":"","content":"I'm just wondering what one would see if the Spoof roll failed, whether it be because of a low cover rating, or something else. I assume you'd just see the cables and the likes... I wonder what stigmatics might look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3910-lord_salamander","name":"Lord_Salamander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T22:20:00-07:00","id":261824,"title":"","content":"There seems to be a general trend (heavy emphasis on &quot;seems to&quot; - my sample points thusfar cover about two and a half supernatural groups) in 2e where &quot;aura&quot; descriptions are moving a bit away from the definite aura-color-and-modifier-chart descriptor methodology and more toward a modus of relevant evocative imagery that can be personalized from character to character.<br /> <br /> That kept in mind, I'd emphasize the stigmata on any aural reading of a stigmatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[